# user-ui Application

Public-facing Angular app at `frontend/projects/user-ui/` (port **5200**). Minimal starter — grow here, not in `admin-ui`.

## Stack

- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS 4 — not Angular Material.
- **Layout:** `MainLayoutComponent` in `shared/layout/main/` wraps page routes.
- **Components:** feature pages under `pages/`; shared widgets under `shared/components/`.

## Structure

```
user-ui/src/app/
  pages/           # Route-level feature components
  shared/          # Layout, spinner, etc.
  core/            # Environment factory
  app.routes.ts    # Top-level routes
```

## Rules

- Keep admin CRUD and Material tables in **admin-ui** — do not copy admin list/edit patterns here.
- When adding API calls: create HTTP services in **common-ui/services/** (extend `BaseApiService`), inject `EnvironmentService.apiUrl`.
- Reuse **common-ui** auth (`AuthSignal`, interceptors, guards) when login is needed — do not fork session storage.
- Follow **angular-20.mdc**: standalone components, signals, `OnPush`, external `.html` (and `.scss` when styles are needed).
- Lazy-load feature routes as the app grows.
- Environment via `window.__env` — see `.cursor/rules/frontend/environment.mdc`.

## Dev

```bash
# From frontend/
ng serve user-ui
```

API base: `http://localhost:8200/v1` (dev `env.js`).
